{%- comment -%}
  Results fragment for "השלימו את הערכה" (snippets/product-addons).

  Fetched as /search?q=<query>&type=product&options[prefix]=last&section_id=product-addons and
  printed as bare tiles; assets/product-addons.js moves them into the matching panel on the product
  page. The shell itself is a snippet, rendered under the gallery inside main-product, so this file
  is only ever the fragment.

  Why search and not collections: the case that fits "iPhone 17 Pro Max" sits inside a 3,390-product
  accessories collection, and Liquid cannot filter a collection by title. The store's titles put the
  model after "ל-" ("כיסוי Apple TechWoven Case ל-iPhone 17 Pro Max שחור"), which the search engine
  indexes, so "כיסוי " + the model is an exact server-side match over the whole catalogue. The
  theme's predictive search uses the same route for the same reason: /search/suggest answers 417 to
  Hebrew on this store.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- if search.performed and search.terms != blank -%}

  {%- comment -%}
    Results fragment. Only accessories are kept: this store prefixes every accessory product type
    with "א." (א.מכשירים, א.רכב, א.אוזניות…), so a brand query like "מטען Apple" cannot drag an iPad
    into a list of chargers.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- paginate search.results by 24 -%}
    {%- assign pa_shown = 0 -%}
    {%- for pa_item in search.results -%}
      {%- liquid
        if pa_shown >= 8
          break
        endif
        assign pa_ok = false
        if pa_item.object_type == 'product'
          if pa_item.available
            assign pa_type = pa_item.type | strip
            assign pa_head = pa_type | slice: 0, 2
            if pa_head == 'א.'
              assign pa_ok = true
            endif
          endif
        endif
      -%}
      {%- if pa_ok -%}
        {%- liquid
          assign pa_variant = pa_item.selected_or_first_available_variant
          assign pa_compare = 0
          if pa_variant.compare_at_price > pa_variant.price
            assign pa_compare = pa_variant.compare_at_price
          endif
          assign pa_shown = pa_shown | plus: 1
        -%}
        <li
          class="pa-card"
          data-pa-item
          data-pa-handle="{{ pa_item.handle }}"
          data-pa-variant="{{ pa_variant.id }}"
          data-pa-price="{{ pa_variant.price }}"
          data-pa-compare="{{ pa_compare }}"
          data-pa-title="{{ pa_item.title | escape }}"
        >
          <label class="pa-card__label">
            <input class="pa-card__check" type="checkbox" data-pa-check>
            {%- comment -%}
              The image comes from all_products[handle], not from the search result. A product inside
              search.results carries its title, type and variants but no image accessor at all —
              featured_image, featured_media and images all came back empty, and every tile rendered
              an empty well twice before this. all_products hands back the real product object, and
              Liquid's limit of 20 such lookups per request is far above the 8 tiles printed here.
            {%- endcomment -%}
            {%- assign pa_full = all_products[pa_item.handle] -%}
            <span class="pa-card__media">
              {%- if pa_full.featured_image != blank -%}
                {%- render 'image',
                  image: pa_full.featured_image,
                  widths: '120,240',
                  sizes: '68px',
                  decorative: true,
                  class: 'pa-card__img'
                -%}
              {%- endif -%}
            </span>
            <span class="pa-card__text">
              <span class="pa-card__title">{{ pa_item.title | escape }}</span>
              <span class="pa-card__prices">
                <span class="pa-card__price">{{ pa_variant.price | money_without_trailing_zeros }}</span>
                {%- if pa_compare > 0 -%}
                  <s class="pa-card__was">{{ pa_compare | money_without_trailing_zeros }}</s>
                {%- endif -%}
              </span>
            </span>
            {%- comment -%}
              Both icons are always in the DOM and the CSS shows one: a "+" to add, a tick once it is
              chosen. It is a drawing, not a control — the label around the real checkbox is what
              takes the click, so there is no button inside a label.
            {%- endcomment -%}
            <span class="pa-card__mark" aria-hidden="true">
              <span class="pa-card__icon pa-card__icon--plus">{%- render 'icon', name: 'plus', size: 16 -%}</span>
              <span class="pa-card__icon pa-card__icon--check">{%- render 'icon', name: 'check', size: 16 -%}</span>
            </span>
          </label>
        </li>
      {%- endif -%}
    {%- endfor -%}
  {%- endpaginate -%}

{%- endif -%}

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "תוספות למוצר (תוצאות)",
  "tag": "div",
  "class": "section-product-addons-results",
  "settings": []
}
{% endschema %}
